From 485708f5a1461d3dfb8109e33d9d7f8964baa6cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <meischris39@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:46:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [games] Start a game from its own media, not saved disc state

Kodi saved each game's disc list, selected disc and tray to
discstate.xml and discstate.m3u in the game's folder, and restored them
the next time the game started, overriding the core's own choice of
startup disc. A game could start on the last disc used or with the tray
open, and an edited playlist was ignored until the saved copy was
deleted.

Drop the saved state, so a game always starts from the file or playlist
it was opened with. Savestates and rewind keep their own disc state.
